A||||9||Wolfhound||RFTH Photos No.1||||14||
Z||000000||Wolfhound||09-24-2001||08:09 AM||||First, let me say that The Run For The Hills gathering was hands down the most fun I,ve ever had with the Fiero. I knew it would be special as the cars began to show up Saturday morning for the run.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rfth01.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rfth02.JPG"> <BR>David Hunter of Alabama Fieros gathered everyone and said "Those who want to go fast go first". This must have been a majority as it precipitated something akin to a Lemans start. For those of you who are unfamilar with the Blue Ridge Parkway, It has beautfully designed sweeping flowing turnssome tight some large that can be viewed across the gaps for maybe a half mile. It was an amazing sight seeing the line of 30+ multicolored fieros stretched around the long turns.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rfth08.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rfth09.JPG"> <BR>Our first stop at Waterlock Knob a large over look in a saddle.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rfth05.JPG"> <BR>The next stop at mount Hardy Parking Overlook.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rfth06.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rfth07.JPG">    ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Nashco||09-24-2001||09:58 AM||||Looks like a good show up of people and a lot of fun!  I wish I could have been there...<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||PAUL88GT||09-24-2001||01:56 PM||||I had a great time.  It was good to finally meet you Wolfhound.  The interior on your SE is really looking super.  Keep up the good work. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ronnie||09-24-2001||07:08 PM||||We got our pics developed today, will post some when I can. The pics really don't tell the whole story . We were probably averaging about 60 mph on a 45 mph road. Did I say averaged?At times I know I hit 70 , then had to brake and geardown for the corners.<BR>Boy, they sure do need to put up some guardrails on some of  those lefties don't they!||||reg||6
Z||000004||Wolfhound||09-24-2001||10:14 PM||||Made my brakes stink gassing on the downhills, Heal and toe.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> My cousin Ken came close to a nervous breakdown, at the first stop he said Thank God, I can take a breath now. I'm not sure I could have handled it as a passenger.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ronnie||09-24-2001||11:02 PM||||Umm , Wolfhound, refresh my memory, which car was yours? Sorry , can't remember.||||reg||9
Z||000006||Bob Englert||09-24-2001||11:44 PM||||I know I couldn't do RFTH as a passenger!  <P>Lyn tried to help me a few times by trying to find a brake pedal on the passenger side to press on!<P><BR>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 09-25-2001).]||||reg||1
